{"file": "D:\\SpaceBook\\_cls7_jpg\\hist\\089.jpg", "lines": [{"text": "Unit: 05The Mughal Empire", "conf": 0.898, "box": [[377, 73], [567, 70], [567, 91], [377, 94]]}, {"text": "Persian name Jahangir, meaning World Seizure' as his title.", "conf": 0.912, "box": [[71, 170], [590, 175], [590, 207], [71, 202]]}, {"text": "Nur-ud-dinJahangir(1605-1628AD)", "conf": 0.921, "box": [[73, 214], [503, 222], [503, 251], [73, 244]]}, {"text": "Nur-ud-din Muhammad Salim often called Prince Salim was the", "conf": 0.912, "box": [[73, 252], [648, 255], [648, 284], [73, 281]]}, {"text": "fourth Mughal Ruler. He was Akbar's son by a Rajput wife. He", "conf": 0.92, "box": [[72, 278], [648, 280], [648, 310], [72, 308]]}, {"text": "ascended throne on his father's death in 1605. His ascension was", "conf": 0.901, "box": [[74, 305], [649, 309], [649, 336], [74, 332]]}, {"text": "challenged by his eldest son Khusrau who revolted against him.", "conf": 0.959, "box": [[75, 331], [649, 334], [649, 363], [75, 360]]}, {"text": "The revolt was put down however it led to execution of fifth Sikh", "conf": 0.873, "box": [[76, 358], [649, 359], [649, 386], [76, 385]]}, {"text": "Guru Arjun Dev. This resulted an increase in tension between", "conf": 0.921, "box": [[76, 384], [650, 387], [650, 414], [76, 411]]}, {"text": "Nur-ud-Din", "conf": 0.761, "box": [[714, 395], [793, 395], [793, 416], [714, 416]]}, {"text": "MughalsandSikhs.", "conf": 0.915, "box": [[79, 414], [260, 414], [260, 434], [79, 434]]}, {"text": "MuhammadSalim", "conf": 0.91, "box": [[688, 414], [818, 411], [818, 432], [688, 434]]}, {"text": "Influenceof NurJahan", "conf": 0.901, "box": [[78, 451], [295, 452], [295, 475], [78, 474]]}, {"text": "Theemperor JahangirwasmarriedtoMehr-un-Nisawhoassumed thetitleof NurJahan.", "conf": 0.926, "box": [[80, 483], [849, 483], [849, 507], [80, 507]]}, {"text": "She was a daughter of one of his ministers. Owing to her beauty and intelligence, she", "conf": 0.91, "box": [[79, 509], [849, 511], [849, 534], [79, 532]]}, {"text": "gained influence on Jahangir and had the opportunity to playa direct role in the affairs of", "conf": 0.919, "box": [[80, 533], [851, 534], [851, 561], [80, 560]]}, {"text": "the empire. She was also actively involved in the political and military affairs. Nur Jahan", "conf": 0.927, "box": [[79, 559], [850, 560], [850, 587], [79, 585]]}, {"text": "became the real power behind the Mughal throne during Jahangir's reign.", "conf": 0.932, "box": [[80, 584], [716, 588], [716, 614], [80, 611]]}, {"text": "Contributions of Nur-ud-din", "conf": 0.905, "box": [[82, 625], [343, 624], [343, 648], [82, 649]]}, {"text": "Do You Know?", "conf": 0.858, "box": [[465, 639], [608, 639], [608, 663], [465, 663]]}, {"text": "MuhammadJahangir", "conf": 0.889, "box": [[82, 652], [288, 652], [288, 675], [82, 675]]}, {"text": "On become successor, Nur-ud-din", "conf": 0.889, "box": [[488, 668], [802, 669], [802, 694], [488, 693]]}, {"text": "TheemperorJahangirwas involved in", "conf": 0.919, "box": [[82, 687], [421, 686], [421, 710], [82, 711]]}, {"text": "MuhammadSalimgave'himself", "conf": 0.924, "box": [[489, 695], [804, 697], [804, 720], [489, 718]]}, {"text": "conquests aimed at expanding the", "conf": 0.861, "box": [[82, 712], [395, 711], [395, 737], [82, 738]]}, {"text": "Persianname Jahangir (World Seizer)", "conf": 0.885, "box": [[489, 721], [803, 722], [803, 745], [489, 744]]}, {"text": "territories under Mughal's rule. He", "conf": 0.914, "box": [[83, 737], [398, 736], [398, 762], [83, 763]]}, {"text": "He permitted the British to trade in", "conf": 0.927, "box": [[491, 754], [808, 755], [808, 779], [491, 778]]}, {"text": "successfullyendedthewarwith the", "conf": 0.941, "box": [[83, 765], [408, 762], [408, 787], [83, 789]]}, {"text": "India which ultimately led to end of", "conf": 0.906, "box": [[489, 780], [814, 780], [814, 806], [489, 806]]}, {"text": "RajputprincedomofMewarin1614", "conf": 0.909, "box": [[85, 792], [412, 788], [413, 811], [85